    {
      "type": "prose",
      "title": "What it is meant to be",
      "data": {
        "body": [
          {
            "en": "KernID is described as a personal identity kernel that unifies a person's digital life under one authentication system: a person signs in once and reaches accounts, digital events and transaction history through a single encrypted vault. The user decides what to share, with whom, and for how long."
          }
